  "name": "ft-asteroids",
  "title": "Flight test: asteroids",
  "description": "Fly the twin-engine ship among slowly drifting asteroids. Each pulls you with its own gravity, and the arena wraps round: leave one edge and you come back at the other. The propellant lasts 20 times as long as it would (an engine economy setting the ledger records as supply), so you can fly for minutes. Nothing is scripted and nothing ends the run: bump into a rock and you bounce. On a touch screen use the buttons on the view; on a keyboard, Q fires left and E fires right.",
